<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_risk" target="ai_data_backlash::reg_enforcement_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising risk of gas/electricity shortfalls triggers regulators to impose and enforce energy‑use restrictions, reporting requirements and compliance checks on energy‑intensive data centers and AI operations, raising the pace of formal enforcement actions.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_data_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_risk" target="iran_gulf_escalation::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased risk of disruption to oil and gas flows from the Russia–Ukraine war prompts extra naval escorts, coalition patrols, and force-posturing around chokepoints (e.g., Strait of Hormuz), which raises incident risk and diplomatic friction in the Iran–Gulf theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
