<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::partisan_polarization" target="ai_data_backlash::political_investigations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified partisan competition drives political actors to weaponize oversight bodies and prosecutors to open investigations into opponents, increasing the volume and intensity of political probes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_data_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::partisan_polarization" target="ai_data_backlash::media_scandal_coverage" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Polarized audiences and partisan outlets amplify allegations and competition for attention, producing a higher volume and prominence of scandal-focused coverage.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_data_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::partisan_polarization" target="iran_gulf_escalation::oversight_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger US partisan polarization increases congressional incentives to use high‑profile hearings and oversight of executive Iran/Gulf policy (to score political points), producing more frequent and aggressive legislative scrutiny of incidents and responses in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::partisan_polarization" target="us_political_realign::policy_signal_coherence" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Growing partisan division produces conflicting public statements, legislative proposals, and oversight actions from rival political camps about China policy, directly degrading the consistency and clarity of official policy signals.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_realign</data>
</edge>
