</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::regional_conflict_level" target="ai_data_backlash::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating military and strategic tensions increase national-security concerns that prompt regulators to widen and intensify scrutiny of data flows, AI exports and related corporate practices.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_data_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::regional_conflict_level" target="iran_gulf_escalation::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in US–China military incidents and deterrence posturing reallocates diplomatic and military alignments (e.g., deeper China–Iran security cooperation and louder Chinese diplomatic cover), which directly emboldens Iranian Gulf-facing operations and raises the frequency/intensity of incidents in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::regional_conflict_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::security_incident_freque" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalation in US–China regional confrontations (e.g., Taiwan Strait) draws US/NATO operational and diplomatic focus and can cause redeployment or delayed support to Ukraine, which Russian forces opportunistically exploit to increase the tempo and number of strikes and incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::regional_conflict_level" target="us_political_realign::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalation of kinetic or near‑kinetic incidents in a regional theatre (e.g., increased PLA sorties, naval standoffs, or missile tests) precipitates allied force deployments, reciprocal diplomatic measures, and sanctions that raise the overall level of interstate strategic rivalry and diplomatic strain.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_realign</data>
</edge>
