  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">High-profile media exposés that firms or governments supplied surveillance, data or dual-use AI to Iranian actors prompt sanctions, diplomatic expulsions and retaliatory messaging/actions that raise Iran–Gulf tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_data_backlash</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_data_backlash::media_scandal_coverage" target="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">High‑profile media exposés about AI firms prompt rapid portfolio shifts and risk repricing (investor flight from tech into commodities and defence equities), producing short‑term spikes in volatility in energy and commodity markets that materially affect financial and commodity price uncertainty tied to the war.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_data_backlash</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_data_backlash::media_scandal_coverage" target="us_china_strategic_rival::partisan_polarization" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">High‑volume scandal reporting about AI/data misuse amplifies polarized narratives and pressure on political actors to adopt harder or more protectionist stances on China, increasing domestic partisan division over China policy.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_data_backlash</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
