<edge source="us_political_realign::policy_signal_coherence" target="ai_data_backlash::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Clear, consistent public policy signals reduce regulators' need to expand investigatory reviews and ad-hoc oversight, so an increase in coherence directly lowers immediate regulatory scrutiny of sectors like AI.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_data_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_realign::policy_signal_coherence" target="iran_gulf_escalation::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Improved coherence and consistency of US policy signals (clear red lines, deconfliction channels, allied messaging) reduces misperception and unintended escalation, lowering the rate of incidents and diplomatic frictions in the Iran–Gulf theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_realign::policy_signal_coherence" target="russia_ukraine_war::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Clear, consistent US policy signals on military/financial support and sanctions reduce investor ambiguity about future exposures in war‑affected assets and commodities, directly lowering price swings in related markets; the reverse (incoherence) raises volatility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_realign::policy_signal_coherence" target="us_china_strategic_rival::partisan_polarization" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">More coherent, consistent public policy signals reduce opportunities for opponents to frame divergent narratives about China policy, thereby lowering incentives for partisan theatricalization and cross-party escalation on the issue.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
